Energy is hitting new all-time highs.

This is exactly why cycles matter.

Leadership changes as the business cycle evolves, and late-cycle energy strength can have consequences far beyond energy itself:

Higher energy → inflation pressure → tighter monetary policy → pressure on long-duration assets.

@MatthewHyland_ Late cycle can last years. Late cycle is characterized by narrow leadership and low unemployment which is where we are now

@MatthewHyland_ in fact, since the Fed is likely about to raise rates, it implies the economy is doing just fine right now. I would not mistake "late cycle" for "the cycle is over"

@MatthewHyland_ I have been bullish on energy all year and remain bullish on it for next 1-2 years so I think we are on the same page.

